  "slug": "mass-proteomics-8cb8",
  "summary": "Seven preprints deliver QC, annotation and analysis tools spanning imaging, lipidomics, metabolomics and proteomics, with an emphasis on accessibility.",
  "synthesis": "The shared thread is the standardization of downstream mass spectrometry data handling rather than new acquisition principles. Several tools are R Shiny apps: LipidRT uses retention time coherence to validate and expand lipid annotations in reversed-phase LC-MS, OSMSS provides no-code differential abundance, phosphosite and enrichment analyses for proteomics, and MetaboRx combines quality metrics with preprocessing for metabolomics. msiFlow 2.0 adds mass recalibration, lipid annotation, batch correction and visual QC to an imaging pipeline. QC Shotgun defines eight relative metrics for benchmarking instrument performance in shotgun lipidomics. MSGFLEX pairs MS-GF+ with XPECTRA XGBoost rescoring to raise peptide and protein identifications in proteomics and metaproteomics. A NanoShield trap column benchmark against PepMap and direct injection addresses low-input proteomics at the hardware-workflow interface.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-25"
}
